The calendar sheet ran on Gregorian months in both languages and could
browse endlessly into months the sync never fetched. Under Persian it now
runs on the Solar Hijri calendar (ported jalaali algorithms in
src/lib/jalali.ts, pinned against Intl's ca-persian in tests/jalali.test.ts),
and navigation clamps to today ± 3 months in the active calendar. The feed
query widened to that range (server clamp ceiling 300→2000 for explicit
range queries) so picked far days show real fixtures and the sheet's dots
cover them, and a daily horizon sweep (~95 days) backfills fixtures beyond
the routine 21-day lookahead, on boot, daily cron and `npm run sync --
horizon`.

